            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences awarded the 2017 Nobel Prize for Chemistry to Jacques Dubochet, Joachim Frank, and Richard Henderson for &quot;developing cryoelectron microscopy for the high-resolution structure determination of biomolecules in solution.&quot; Achieving this goal, which required innovation, persistence, and uncommon physical insight, has broadened horizons for structural studies in molecular and cell biology.</AbstractText>
